ROLE
You are a senior front-end engineer and an AODA / WCAG 2.0 AA accessibility expert
(also apply WCAG 2.1/2.2 AA best practices). Build the feature below in
[TECHNOLOGY: e.g. GWT 2.x with Java + UiBinder / React / Angular / plain HTML5+JS].

GOAL
Build a page with a data table and asynchronous, stacking notification popups
that never cover the table. They must be fully accessible and adapt to screen
size, device and zoom level.

1. MAIN PAGE
- A data table with [10] rows and [5] columns of dummy data about [books]
  (Title, Author, Genre, Year, Pages).
- Semantic table: caption, <th scope="col"> headers, and a row header in the first column.
- The table sits in a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll region so it can
  scroll horizontally inside itself without making the page scroll sideways.
- When no popup exists, the page uses its ORIGINAL layout. Nothing is reserved,
  padded or shrunk permanently.

2. NOTIFICATION POPUPS
- A new popup appears every [15] seconds, triggered by an async source
  (timer here; in production a WebSocket, server push or RPC callback).
- Default position: floating in the bottom-right corner of the viewport.
- Stacking: each new popup goes BEHIND the existing ones, offset [10px] upward,
  so a thin strip of each older popup stays visible. The oldest is in front.
  - All popups in the stack have equal height so the strip is always visible.
  - Show at most [4] layers visually. Extra popups stay queued and are hidden.
- Only the front popup is interactive. Popups behind it are aria-hidden and
  inert (not focusable, not announced).
- Each popup shows: "Notification X of N", a title, a message, and buttons:
  Primary action ("View in table"), Dismiss, and Dismiss all (only when N > 1).
- Popups never auto-dismiss.
- A user-controlled "Pause new notifications" toggle (aria-pressed) stops new
  popups (WCAG 2.2.2).

3. ADAPTIVE PLACEMENT (dynamic, not permanent)
Run this on: popup added, popup removed, window resize, zoom, and rotation.

  If there are no popups:
      restore the original layout (clear any table width override, return the
      stack to the floating corner position).
  Otherwise measure (all in CSS px; use rem so browser zoom is respected):
      originalW  = content width of the table's container with no override
      left       = left edge of the table's container
      popupW     = min(22.5rem, viewportWidth - 2rem)
      popupLeft  = viewportWidth - 1rem - popupW
      limit      = popupLeft - 16px gap
      avail      = limit - left
  Decide placement:
      A. NONE   - if the table's right edge <= limit: change nothing.
      B. SHRINK - else if avail >= MIN_TABLE_RATIO * originalW (default 0.70):
                  set the table container's max-width to avail. Only the
                  container shrinks. The table scrolls horizontally inside it
                  if needed.
      C. BELOW  - else: clear any shrink and move the popup stack out of the
                  floating position into normal document flow directly BELOW
                  the table, right-aligned to the screen, with extra top
                  margin for the stacking offsets. Show a visible "Go to
                  notifications below the table (N)" button in the page header.
  Rules:
      - MIN_TABLE_RATIO is a single named constant, so it is easy to change.
      - Add ~5% hysteresis when leaving BELOW so a scrollbar appearing or
        disappearing cannot cause flip-flopping.
      - Decisions are based on width only, so scrolling never triggers reflow.
      - Batch recalculation (e.g. one animation frame / scheduler) to avoid layout thrash.
      - If focus is inside the stack when it moves in the DOM, restore focus to
        the same control afterward.

4. ACCESSIBILITY REQUIREMENTS (AODA / WCAG 2.0 AA, plus 2.1/2.2 best practice)
- Live region: a role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" element must
  exist in the DOM at page load. Announce "New notification. <title>. <message>.
  You now have N notifications. Press Alt+N to review." Also announce dismiss,
  dismiss-all, pause and resume. Send all async events through ONE announce()
  function. Reset the region's text and re-set it after ~100 ms so repeated
  messages are re-announced.
- Never move focus when a popup appears (3.2.1).
- Landmark: <aside aria-label="Notifications">. Each popup is role="group"
  with aria-labelledby and aria-describedby.
- Keyboard:
    - Alt+N and a "Skip to notifications" skip link focus the front popup.
    - Esc inside the notifications dismisses the front popup.
    - Every function is reachable by keyboard in a logical order.
- Focus management: when the focused popup is removed, move focus to the next
  popup's first button, or back to the last element focused outside the stack,
  or else to <main tabindex="-1">. Focus must never fall back to <body>.
- Focus visibility: visible focus ring on EVERY interactive element using
  :focus (not only :focus-visible), >= 3px, with contrast >= 3:1 against the
  adjacent colour on both light and dark surfaces.
- Contrast: text >= 4.5:1; UI components >= 3:1. Never use colour alone.
- Target size >= 44x44 CSS px.
- Reflow: no two-dimensional page scroll at 320px or 400% zoom, except inside
  the table's own scroll region. Popups limited to ~45% viewport height with
  internal scroll.
- Motion: respect prefers-reduced-motion. No flashing.
- Support forced-colors mode.
- Skip links for main content and notifications.
- Set the page language, e.g. lang="en-CA".
- Insert dynamic text as text, never as HTML (XSS-safe).
- Use real <button> elements with accessible names.

5. DELIVERABLES
- Complete source for [TECHNOLOGY], runnable as-is.
- A short explanation of how the layout algorithm maps onto this technology.
- A manual test checklist (below) with expected results.
- A list of assumptions and the tunable constants.

6. ACCEPTANCE TESTS (state pass/fail for each)
  a. No popup: table width and layout are identical to the original.
  b. Wide desktop, popup appears: either NONE or SHRINK. No pixel of the
     table is covered. On dismiss, the table returns to its original width.
  c. Tablet / mid-width: SHRINK up to 30%, then BELOW once the reduction would
     exceed that.
  d. Phone / 400% zoom: BELOW mode, popups right-aligned under the table, and
     the header button appears.
  e. Resize or zoom while popups are shown: placement updates without reload.
  f. Screen reader (NVDA/JAWS/VoiceOver): the arrival of each popup is
     announced once; popups behind are not read; no focus theft.
  g. Keyboard only: Tab, Alt+N, Esc, Dismiss all and pause work; focus is
     always visible and never lost.
  h. Pause stops new popups; resume restarts them; both are announced.
  i. Automated scan (axe/WAVE) shows no violations. Manual review is still done.

CONSTRAINTS
- Don't add libraries unless [TECHNOLOGY] needs them.
- Keep all tunables (INTERVAL_MS, MAX_LAYERS, STACK_OFFSET_PX, MIN_TABLE_RATIO,
  GAP_PX, POPUP_WIDTH_REM) as named constants at the top.
- Comment the non-obvious accessibility decisions.









GWT NOTES
- Use GWT [2.10+] with UiBinder, or plain Widgets. Target Java 11.
- Put the live region and <aside> in the host HTML page so they exist at load.
- Wrap DOM access in JsInterop (elemental2 / gwt-elemental) or JSNI.
- Use ResizeObserver via JsInterop if available, plus Window.addResizeHandler,
  and schedule the layout with Scheduler.get().scheduleFinally.
  getComputedStyle, getBoundingClientRect and clientWidth should be read through
  JsInterop, not guessed from Widget sizes.
- Emit all async events (RPC callbacks, EventBus, Timer) through one
  NotificationService with methods add(), dismissFront(), dismissAll(),
  setPaused() and relayout(). Presenters call this service, not the DOM.
- Use CssResource (with @external for class names toggled from script) for
  styles. Use a Messages interface for all user-facing strings so they can be
  localized (en-CA / fr-CA).
- Keep layout and focus logic out of views; a pure Java class holding the
  placement decision (NONE/SHRINK/BELOW) can be JUnit-tested with plain numbers.
- Use GWTTestCase only where DOM behaviour must be verified.




